## Example Usage

Exocompute is configured per region, using one `regional_config` block for each region the cluster should run in. The
GKE pods use the `pods-cidr-range` secondary IP range on the subnet, unless another range is specified with the
`secondary_range_name` field:

{{tffile .ExampleFile}}

To run Exocompute on a Shared VPC, where the VPC network belongs to a separate host project, specify the host project
using the `host_project_id` field. Note, this is the GCP project ID of the host project, not the RSC cloud account ID,
which is why the example below reads `project_id` and not `id` from the `polaris_gcp_project` data source:

{{tffile "examples/resources/polaris_gcp_exocompute/shared-vpc.tf"}}
{{end}}

